st-4/runbooks/README.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n exited 1 in 0ms:\n# Product brief \u2014 Mock Fantasy Quest 4\n\n**Source of truth:** [`INITIAL.md`](INITIAL.md). This normalized brief supports\ndownstream planning; it preserves source scope and records unknowns rather than\nchoosing them.\n\n## Product problem and outcome\n\nCasual adult players need a compact, approachable fantasy RPG that delivers a\ncomplete story without requiring a long commitment or dependable connection.\nThe first useful session is successful when a new player finishes a first\nturn-based battle and understands how to save and resume. The release outcome\nis an original short campaign that a player can complete through exploration,\ndialogue, quests, combat, rewards, saving, and a short ending.\n\n## Category, users, and core experience\n\n| Area | Normalized first-release statement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Category | Deliberately small, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG. |\n| Users | Casual and adult players, including people using keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad, captions, adjustable text, and visual settings. |\n| Campaign boundary | One town, one dungeon, and one guided, short ending; no further regions or chapters are required. |\n| Core loop | Explore, converse, accept or advance a quest, enter party-based turn-based combat, manage rewards/inventory, save, and continue. |\n| Experience direction | Original warm hand-painted fantasy, readable silhouettes, and a restrained palette. |\n| Functional reference | *Final Fantasy V* may inform only the high-level scope of a party-based turn-based adventure. |\n\n## Selected target systems\n\n| Target | First-release role | Input model | Delivery constraints | Out-of-scope boundary |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Responsive public web application | Primary browser surface for the complete game. | Keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad. | Responsive phone/tablet/desktop layout; browser compatibility and performance budget must be approved before implementation. | Native binaries, a separate web-only campaign, and browser-exclusive mechanics. |\n| Progressive web app (PWA) | Installable delivery of the same shared game core. | Same inputs where the browser/device supports them. | Offline assets and save-data behavior; safe update/cache refresh must preserve confirmed player data. | A PWA-exclusive campaign, mandatory continuous connection, or a different ruleset. |\n\nThe product uses a shared core with platform adaptation only where necessary.\nIt should work on widely used devices and under feasible slow-network\nconditions; exact supported browsers, device classes, storage quotas, and\nnetwork floor are open decisions.\n\n## First-release scope and measurable success measures\n\nIncluded scope: playable exploration; one town and one dungeon; narrative,\ndialogue, quests, progression and a short ending; onboarding/tutorial; at least\none tutorialized turn-based battle; inventory and rewards; save/load, resume,\ncheckpoints, data-loss recovery; settings and accessibility; audio/visual\nfeedback; content/level delivery; and crash reporting with player-facing error\nrecovery. The source also names account/identity, multiplayer/player safety,\nlive-service operations, and purchase/entitlement handling, but their release\nstatus remains contingent on the explicit conflict decision below.\n\nThe release is measurable when:\n\n- A new player can finish the tutorial battle, create a save, reload it, and\n  reach the short ending on each supported target.\n- The delivered campaign contains exactly one town, one dungeon, and one short\n  ending; added regions or chapters are not needed for release completion.\n- Both targets meet their stated input role; the PWA is installable and each\n  target has a tested offline, save, update, and error-recovery path.\n- Dialogue, inventory, quest, and progression UI are readable with approved\n  accessibility settings, and captions/visual settings are available where the\n  corresponding feedback exists.\n- An interruption, recoverable error, or safe update offers a player-facing\n  recovery path and does not silently discard the last confirmed save.\n\n## Later roadmap, non-goals, and reference boundary\n\nDeferred roadmap: live events/seasonal content, player-created/shared content\n(levels, mods, designs, stories), advanced analytics, and advanced\nmonetisation. They are excluded from first-release acceptance.\n\nNon-goals: copied branding, assets, text, layouts, characters, story/lore,\naudio, maps, or distinctive interactions; additional towns/dungeons/campaigns;\nnative apps; and platform-specific game variants. No cloud-sync, payment,\nmoderation, service-uptime, or backend commitment is implied before approval.\n\n| Reference boundary | Prohibited | Permitted |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Branding and copy | Names, logos, trademarks, marketing copy, story text, dialogue, characters, and world/lore. | A high-level description of a compact party-based turn-based adventure. |\n| Assets and presentation | Art, music, sound, maps, screen composition, visual language, and layouts. | Original art and UI that fulfil this brief\u2019s own direction. |\n| Interaction design | Reproducing distinctive combat screens, menus, flows, quests, or interaction choreography. | Independently designed mechanics and feedback appropriate to the requested scope. |\n\n## Constraints and safe assumptions\n\nExplicit constraints: web/PWA delivery, offline play, accessibility,\nlocalisation, privacy, safe save/recovery, slow-network feasibility, and\noriginal expression. Safe working assumptions: the offline core does not block\non a remote service; content/UI are original; local persistence is durable\nenough for confirmed saves where browser storage permits; connected features,\nif approved, degrade visibly; and crash diagnostics minimize personal data.\nThese are guardrails, not approval of a stack, vendor, backend, account model,\ndata-retention policy, or technical promise.\n\n## Open decisions requiring human approval\n\n1. **Offline versus connected scope:** Reconcile the offline single-player\n   premise with required account identity, multiplayer safety, live operations,\n   and purchase/entitlement handling. Classify each as release-critical,\n   optional connected enhancement, or deferred.\n2. **Account and data policy:** Decide whether accounts are absent, optional,\n   or mandatory; then define authentication, sync/conflict behavior, retention,\n   deletion, and offline/service-outage recovery.\n3. **Multiplayer, commerce, and safety:** State whether multiplayer or\n   real-money purchases actually ship, plus age rating, regions, moderation,\n   reporting, refunds, store, and applicable legal obligations.\n4. **Technical delivery baseline:** Choose engine/framework, repository and CI\n   constraints, browser/device matrix, performance budget, offline-storage\n   quota, update activation policy, error-reporting provider, and cost model.\n5. **Production content and access:** Approve party size, encounter/quest\n   counts, combat/progression balance, language set, audio scope, and the exact\n   accessibility options before production planning.\n# Canonical specification index\n\nThis directory is the canonical, resumable specification for **mock-fantasy-quest-4**. It consolidates F001\u2013F010 without overriding [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md), which remains the source of truth. A later author must cite stable IDs here rather than rediscovering scope.\n\n## Control rules\n\n- **P0** is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG: one town, one dungeon, a short guided campaign and ending, exploration, dialogue/quests, party turn combat, inventory, local saves/recovery, settings/accessibility, responsive web, and PWA distribution.\n- Target-neutral rules live in `requirements.*`; the web/PWA differences live in `platform-appendix.md`. PWA is a delivery adaptation of the shared game, not a second game.\n- `Final Fantasy V` is a functional scope reference for party-based turn adventure only. It permits no copied expression: names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts, UI flows, or interaction choreography.\n- `proposed` requirements and every `GATE-*` are not implementation authorisation. Resolve their linked `DEC-*` record before allocating dependent work.\n\n## Chapter register\n\n| Chapter ID | Document / owner | Depends on | State |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SPEC-00 | `00-domain-discovery.md` / product discovery | INITIAL | complete |\n| SPEC-01 | `01-product-brief.md` / product | SPEC-00 | complete |\n| SPEC-02 | `02-feature-model.md` / game design | SPEC-00\u201301 | complete |\n| SPEC-03 | `03-technical-contract.md` / technical design | SPEC-00\u201302 | complete |\n| SPEC-04 | `04-experience-contract.md` / experience design | SPEC-00\u201303 | complete |\n| SPEC-11 | `requirements.md`, `requirements.json` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-00\u201304, planning 05\u201310 | complete |\n| SPEC-12 | `traceability-matrix.md` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-11 | complete; runbook IDs pending F012+ |\n| SPEC-13 | `decision-log.md` / product owner | SPEC-00\u201304 | open decisions recorded |\n| SPEC-14 | `platform-appendix.md` / technical + experience owner | SPEC-11 | complete; thresholds gated |\n| SPEC-15 | `domain-completeness-review.md` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-00\u201304, SPEC-11 | complete; gated domains retained |\n\n## Bounded expansion protocol\n\nExpand one domain chapter at a time, preserving IDs and this register: identify entities/rules, authoring inputs, dependencies, P0 boundary, target adaptations, verification, and open decisions. Proposed detailed chapters are shell/session, campaign content, combat, progression/inventory, persistence/recovery, experience/accessibility, PWA/release, and connected-scope holds. A chapter can move from `planned` to `complete` only when its requirements, trace rows, and decision/risk links exist; it never closes a human gate.\n{\n  \"manifest_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-runbook-authoring-ledger\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"purpose\": \"Persistent, append-only allocation ledger for bounded B-series authoring batches and immutable R-series implementation contracts. It allocates the current catalogue only; queued shards remain expansion work.\",\n  \"project_slug\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4\",\n  \"source_catalogue\": \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\n  \"expected_runbook_count\": 12,\n  \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n  \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\n  \"catalogue_disposition\": {\"allocated\": [\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"], \"deferred\": [], \"human_gates_retained\": {\"IMP-0001\":\"GATE-0001\", \"IMP-0006\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0007\":\"GATE-0003\", \"IMP-0009\":\"GATE-0005\", \"IMP-0010\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004\"}},\n  \"queued_expansion\": [\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 2 after GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand into bounded IMP records before assigning any R IDs\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 3 after GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand after its predecessor shards; preserve shared UI and web-adapter ownership\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"state\":\"queued\",\"future_wave\":\"wave 4 after GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"allocation_rule\":\"expand only after the session/UI and campaign contracts exist\"},\n    {\"chapter\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"state\":\"hold\",\"future_wave\":\"only if explicitly authorised after GATE-0006\",\"allocation_rule\":\"no P0 implementation R contracts\"}\n  ],\n  \"context_packet_baseline\": {\n    \"terminology\": [\"B-series = authoring runbook\", \"R-series = generated implementation runbook\", \"IMP-series = catalogue contract\", \"shared core\", \"web adapter\", \"PWA delivery adapter\", \"local save\", \"cache\", \"human gate\"],\n    \"target_constraints\": [\"original offline-capable 2D single-player RPG\", \"responsive web and installable PWA\", \"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad\", \"no accounts, sync, multiplayer, purchases, or network services in P0\", \"shared core must not import platform/render/network modules\", \"PWA cache and save data remain separate\"],\n    \"required_templates\": [\"runbooks/TEMPLATE.md\", \"runbooks/F014.md provenance and asset-assessment requirements\"],\n    \"authoring_rules\": [\"write only assigned paths\", \"preserve gates and unanswered questions\", \"do not create incidental assets when asset_impact is not_applicable\", \"perform structural, not product-release, validation\"]\n  },\n  \"batches\": [\n    {\"id\":\"B0001\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Bootstrap decision-gated foundation\",\"state\":\"blocked_on_gate\",\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package manager, and CI selection\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0001\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/platform-appendix.md\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0001\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate R0001 metadata and output ownership, record gate disposition, then checkpoint wave\",\"recovery\":\"keep R0001 reserved; after the gate, rerun B0001 only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"one bounded R runbook\",\"gate is explicit\",\"baseline command and ownership evidence are specified\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0002\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"Shared seams, deterministic harness, and token contract\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0001\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0001 accepted; R0012's visual-token portion remains blocked by GATE-0002,GATE-0004\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0010\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0010\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate the three contracts and record any gate-blocked subwork\",\"recovery\":\"repair only R0002,R0003,R0010; never split or renumber accepted contracts\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"core/adapter seam precedes feature work\",\"fixture and token outputs have distinct ownership\",\"all gates retained\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0003\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"Deterministic state slice and connected-scope exclusion\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0002\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0002 accepted\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0004\",\"R0008\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0008\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate state/event ownership and negative connected-scope coverage\",\"recovery\":\"retain IDs and repair the failed R contract only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"vertical foundation slice remains independently reviewable\",\"P0 connected-service exclusion is explicit\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0004\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Content validation and local recovery protocols\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0003 accepted; R0006 requires GATE-0003\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate content/save boundaries and retained storage gate\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0005,R0006 and rerun the blocked item after its decision\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"content and save/cache ownership is separated\",\"save recovery remains a bounded foundation slice\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0005\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Migration, diagnostics, and provenance controls\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0006 after B0004 acceptance, except R0007 still waits for R0006\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0007 needs GATE-0003; R0009 needs GATE-0005\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0007\",\"R0009\",\"R0011\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0011\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate migration, diagnostics, and provenance fields; record unresolved gates\",\"recovery\":\"rerun only incomplete assigned IDs; preserve any accepted R contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no transport or remote diagnostics is introduced\",\"provenance review is explicit\",\"contracts remain at most three\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"B0006\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"Foundation documentation closure\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\",\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0005 after B0004 acceptance\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0006 must be accepted or documented as blocked; no gate is implicitly resolved\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0012\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0012\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"cross-check all foundation ownership, dependencies, and gates before accepting the wave\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0012 and correct only its documentation contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documentation concludes the foundation slice without claiming implementation or approval\",\"gated save work remains visible\"]}\n  ],\n  \"r_contracts\": [\n    {\"id\":\"R0001\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"dependencies\":[],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0001\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documented deterministic baseline command\",\"isolated ownership directories\",\"GATE-0001 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and path; repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0002\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#dependency-direction-and-state-rules\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0002\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; this is an interface and dependency-policy contract.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"forbidden core imports rejected\",\"adapter command-only fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0003\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#observability-quality-evidence-and-release-verification\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0003\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; fixtures use non-product deterministic data.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"repeatable fixture result\",\"isolated fixture storage\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0004\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0004\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"stale and invalid commands do not mutate state\",\"duplicate interaction is idempotent\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0005\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No